            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The dynamics of the IO thermocline cooling is still a topic of debate. Proposed processes include decadal variability\u2079, a shoaling of the western Pacific thermocline induced by a weakening of the easterly trade winds, a southward shift and spin-up of the subtropical gyre \u2075,\u2076,\u2079,\u00b9\u2070, as well as a direct influence from the Indonesian Throughflow (ITF), wherein the Pacific transmits a coastally trapped oceanic upwelling Rossby wave to the tropical IO\u2075,\u00b9\u00b9,\u00b9\u00b2.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Pacific Walker circulation",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Pacific Ocean",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Another potential factor is the weakening of the Pacific Walker circulation, which may be forced by both GHG emissions and natural variability\u00b9\u2075,\u00b9\u2076. However, while some modelling studies suggest the Pacific had very little impact on the subsurface IO prior to the 1990s\u2079,\u00b9\u2077, future surface warming in the tropical and subtropical Pacific may lead to wind-induced redistributions of upper ocean water and a shoaling thermocline in the southern I0\u00b9\u2078.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
